From 6813391d8ae691e6aa8383a0da58ae4f6bf79556 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orlfman <25542856+orlfman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:08:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] linux: add AMDGPU sysfs sampler for RX 9070 XT meters

Read the data for the upcoming RX 9070 XT header meters from sysfs:
GPU, memory controller and video engine busy percentages, VRAM use,
power and power cap, edge/junction/memory temperatures with their
critical limits, and the GPU and memory clocks from hwmon. RDNA 4 has
no pp_dpm_vclk/pp_dpm_dclk, so the video clocks are taken from the
gpu_metrics v1.3 table, after checking its size and revision.

The card is found by PCI ID among the devices bound to amdgpu, and the
hwmon inputs by their labels, since card and hwmon numbers change
between boots. All meters share one sample that is read at most once
per refresh. Nothing is read while the card is runtime suspended, as
reading hwmon or pp_dpm_mclk would wake it up.

Discovery is retried rather than done once: while no card is found it
is looked for on every refresh, a card that is no longer bound to
amdgpu is forgotten and looked for again, and the hwmon directory is
searched until it exists and again whenever it goes away (e.g. when it
is renumbered). The meters thus recover when amdgpu binds the card or
re-registers hwmon after htop started. The values read only once (VRAM
total, memory clock levels, temperature limits, sensor labels) only
count as read when all of them are there, so one that failed to read
is tried again on the next refresh.

AMDGPU_SYSFS_ROOT allows pointing the sampler at a fake sysfs tree for
testing; htop itself always uses /sys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Makefile.am    |   2 +
 linux/AMDGPU.c | 373 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 linux/AMDGPU.h |  64 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 439 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 linux/AMDGPU.c
 create mode 100644 linux/AMDGPU.h

